KG42.register("rules-a63276dfa859bdbaab277f86",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R006","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"PV prosumers may participate as buyers; the source assigns buyer operation when generation does not exceed consumption. Scope: Buyer-role participation of PV prosumers within the microgrid, evaluated per time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Buyer-role participation of PV prosumers within the microgrid, evaluated per time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e012"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x-n","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in one time slot; identified by the source as the decision variable of ESM.","kind":"operational","domain":"x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-Eg-n","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by PV prosumer n in one time slot.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"PV prosumers may participate as buyers; the source assigns buyer operation when generation does not exceed consumption. Scope: Buyer-role participation of PV prosumers within the microgrid, evaluated per time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","expression":"E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x-n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-Eg-n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e012"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e004","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"Here a prosumer is an entity who consumes power and mean while produces power at a certain time. A p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Here a prosumer is an entity who consumes power and meanwhile produces power at a certain time. A prosumer can be any smart buildings, factories or houses which are deployed with PV systems. During the different time periods, the prosumer may behave as a seller or a buyer depending on the circumstance and the net power profile. In this regard, the energy trading inside the microgrid is more likely to be represented as energy sharing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p01-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"NOMENCLATURE","anchor_text":"NSACTIONS ON INDUSTRIAL INFORMATICS, VOL. 13, NO. 3, JUNE 2017 gement for Microgrids With ckelberg G","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"B, S Set of buyers and sellers. E^b, E^s Total trading energy of buyers and sellers. E_n^g Energy produced by prosumer n. G Set of PV prosumers. k_n Preference parameter of prosumer n. N Number of prosumers. N_B, N_S Number of buyers and sellers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Utility Model of PV Prosumers","anchor_text":"revenue of trading energy. In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for differ","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, the prosumers can act as either seller or buyer for different time slots, so we have extended the utility function as a piecewise function: U_n(x_n) = { k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_s(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n > 0; k_n ln(1 + x_n) + p_b(E_n^g − x_n), E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. } (1) In (1), U_n(x_n) is the utility of prosumer n, k_n ln(1 + x_n) is the utility that the prosumer n achieves from consuming energy x_n. Note that k_n is the preference parameter of prosumer n, which changes with behavioral characteristics of the prosumer. It is shown in (1) that a prosumer with higher k_n would be more interested in consuming more x_n to attain its maximum utility level compared to a prosumer with lower preference. The ln(·) function has been widely used in economics for modeling the preference ordering of users and for decision making, and also recently been shown to be suitable for designing the utility for power consumers [23]. p_s(E_n^g − x_n) is the revenue that the prosumer receives from selling the rest of its energy, whereas p_b(E_n^g − x_n) is the negative revenue when the prosumer buys energy."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e004","quote":"During the different time periods, the prosumer may behave as a seller or a buyer depending on the circumstance and the net power profile."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","quote":"Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"02b4d71fc3b38e9d0194145d953c35025162642d25496c2dd322fa3bde3dbe70","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The supplied source explicitly defines prosumer n's net energy E_n^g − x_n and assigns buyer operation in the nonpositive branch E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0. The source also identifies x_n as the prosumer's energy-consumption decision variable and E_n^g as PV energy produced by prosumer n. The formalization is limited to this source-stated buyer-role condition; B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x-n","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Consumption x_n enters the net-energy expression E_n^g − x_n, which determines whether the buyer-role condition for participation.consumer holds."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-Eg-n","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"PV production E_n^g is the source-defined production term in the buyer-role condition for participation.consumer."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized condition E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0 defines the buyer-role participation represented by participation.consumer; the frozen graph has no relevant edge for this unary participation fact."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
